                    <history>
                        <origin>
                            <origDate>
                                <date notBefore="1889" notAfter="1913">
                                    The manuscript was written at the time of king <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS7006Menilek">Mǝnilǝk</persName>, who reigned from 1889 to 1913, 
                                    and metropolitan <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6876Matewos">Mātewos X</persName>, who was in tenure from 1889 to 1926. The name of the original owner was 
                                    <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15250WaldaMa">Walda Masqal</persName>, who is mentioned in numerous supplication formulas throughout. 
                                    In one place the name of <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15251WaldaTa">Walda Tābot</persName> is also mentioned.
                                </date>
                            </origDate>
                        </origin>
                        <provenance>                          
                            According to the account on the manuscripts’ provenance given by Tisserant, this manuscript is among those
                            acquired by <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4805Grebaut">Sylvain Grébaut</persName> in <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1216AddisA">ʾAddis ʾAbabā</placeName> 
                            in <date when="1925"/> with funds of
                            <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS14055SaintJ">Jean Saint</persName>. 
                            The manuscripts originated from Šawā (ʾAddis ʾAbabā, Dabra Libānos, Dabra Bǝrhān),
                            Goǧǧām (Dimā Giyorgis, Marṭula Māryām, Dabra Warq) and Bagemdǝr (Gondar, ʾAzazo Takla Hāymānot) and very few from Tǝgrāy.
                        </provenance>
                        <acquisition when="1928">The manuscript entered the library on <date when="1928-04-18">18 April 1928</date>.</acquisition>
                    </history>
                    
